    {
      "id": 7,
      "user": "employee",
      "question": "What's the process to onboard a new vendor and who approves over $10k?",
      "expected_outcome": "answer",
      "expected_source": [
        "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
        "procurement_approval_matrix.md"
      ],
      "actual_outcome": "answer",
      "answer": "Onboarding process for any new vendor expected to receive payment from the company: 1) Request: the business owner submits a new vendor request in the procurement portal with business justification and estimated annual spend. 2) Documentation: the vendor provides a W-9 (or W-8 for non-U.S. vendors), a certificate of insurance, and banking details. 3) Security review: required for any vendor that will access company systems or handle company or customer data; contact IT Security. 4) Approval: the approval level depends on spend, per the procurement approval matrix. 5) Setup: accounts payable creates the vendor record after approval and verifies bank details by call-back to a known phone number. 6) PO issued: a purchase order is issued before work begins for any spend over $2,500.\n\nApprovers over $10k: based on total contract value (annual spend for recurring contracts), $10,001-$50,000 requires the department head plus the finance director; $50,001-$250,000 requires the VP of Finance plus the COO; over $250,000 requires the CFO plus the CEO. Additionally, sole-source purchases over $10,000 require a written justification, and contracts with auto-renewal clauses require legal review regardless of value.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
          "section": "1. When this applies"
        },
        {
          "source": "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
